{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1336385-question-about-paradox-when-fighting-other-supernaturals-or-other-beings-of-strangeness","id":1336385,"title":"Question about Paradox when fighting other Supernaturals or other Beings of Strangeness","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-09-17T17:21:31-07:00","id":1336385,"title":"Question about Paradox when fighting other Supernaturals or other Beings of Strangeness","content":"When a Mage is ambushed by a say a Vampire wanting to taste his or her vitae after discovering such is a mage or a Were-Creature wanting to dispatch the offender getting too close to a Caern, can Mages use vulgar magic paradox free? What about Ghosts or other beings from the Umbra? Does fighting against Changelings cause Paradox? What about Mummies?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 09-17-2019, 08:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T18:48:38-07:00","id":1336414,"title":"","content":"It's all treated as vulgar but with no witnesses.<br /> Still bending the rules of reality regardless of what the target is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T20:11:49-07:00","id":1336434,"title":"","content":"Supernatural creatures don't count as witnesses. So as Dwight noted, vulgar magic w/o witness is likely for most situations. Though this assumes there are no normal witnesses, or you're not in a special place (being in the Umbra) where everything is coincidental, or might count as a Reality Zone for your character's benefit (the heart of a Caern).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T21:40:34-07:00","id":1336486,"title":"","content":"Sorcerers don't count as witnesses but one of the books mentions Techno-Sorcerers (IE: Enlightened Citizens) DO count as sleepers because of conditioning/something like that, but regular Technocrats don't.<br /> <br /> I think that covers basically every creature/entity.<br /> <br /> Also: Tremere Havens count as coincidental for hermetic magick so, go politely tell them to fuck off at their homebase if you ever hear them talking shit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25315-jihelu","name":"Jihelu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T21:47:50-07:00","id":1336488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jihelu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1336385-question-about-paradox-when-fighting-other-supernaturals-or-other-beings-of-strangeness?p=1336486#post1336486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also: Tremere Havens count as coincidental for hermetic magick so, go politely tell them to fuck off at their homebase if you ever hear them talking shit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because that worked out sooo well the other two times it was done......","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T22:12:36-07:00","id":1336492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1336385-question-about-paradox-when-fighting-other-supernaturals-or-other-beings-of-strangeness?p=1336488#post1336488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because that worked out sooo well the other two times it was done......</div> </div> </div> </div>That's because it was the metaplot doing it and not me, Chad McAlpha Mage. (This is all sarcasm btw, you shouldn't raid the Tremere)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25315-jihelu","name":"Jihelu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T23:03:34-07:00","id":1336494,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure the Techno-sorcerer's thing was turned into a Merit in Revised rather than being default as in 2e, but I haven't gone back and checked.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-18T09:06:15-07:00","id":1336572,"title":"","content":"So if your mage character was fighting a Methuselah vampire in an alley in a high population city like Delhi and uses a Forces fireball missing it, if that stray fireball hits the high traffic city road, will that incur heavy paradox? Or will it cause nothing since they didn't SEE who casted it? Or does the Sleepers seeing the fireball by itself will cause a bunch of paradox to be transferred to the mage?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-18T10:09:35-07:00","id":1336583,"title":"","content":"1\u00ba Seeing the caster has nothing to do with Vulgarity. Vulgarity it's determined by the nature of the effect and the place where the Effect takes place.<br /> <br /> Attacking a Ghost with a spiritual fireball that exists and takes effect <u>only </u>in the Umbra it's going to be Coincident regardless if the caster it's on Earth or on the Umbra.<br /> <br /> For the same reason tossing fireballs to Earth from the Umbra it's going to be Vulgar, even when no one can see the source.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">So if your mage character was fighting a Methuselah vampire in an alley in a high population city like Delhi and uses a Forces fireball missing it, if that stray fireball hits the high traffic city road, will that incur heavy paradox?</div> </div> </div> </div>Effects can't be retroactively Paradoxical.<br /> <br /> If it was adjudicated by the ST that the effect it's Vulgar w/o Witnesses because there was no one in the alley, then it's still so if a sleeper sees it taking place for whatever reason.<br /> <br /> Perhaps the ST should have taken the &quot;range&quot; of the Effect in count before deciding that it's Vulgar w/o Witnesses. And state that it's only going to be so if the ball *can't* possibly be seen (this can be solved by saying that the range it's smaller than the alley, the ball extinguishes before leaving it).<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> In the specific case of a fireball, one could argue that seeing a gout of flame coming out of an alley isn't so terrible from the pov of Vulgarity. &quot;Something&quot; could have exploded and caused the fire to emerge, you don't know what caused it but it doesn't <i>need to be magick</i>. That way one could say that there's no reason to make the fireball more Vulgar than it already was inside<br /> <br /> However, if instead of something easily explainable, what was hitting the trafic out of the alley was<i> in itself</i> impossible (say, a dancing, singing, phoenix of pure fire), we do have this problem. <br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> A possible house-ruling:<br /> <br /> This situation is similar to a rule about Sanctums that can be found in Guide to the Traditions.<br /> <br /> The rule stated that evidently Vulgar effects casted as Coincidental taking advantage of the protection of a Sanctum couldn't exist outside their protection. Such effects would instantly end in case of getting out of the Sanctum paradox-free area ... unless they were specificly casted as Vulgar (with Paradox included). You had to &quot;prepare&quot; the effect as Vulgar if you wanted to carry it outside, otherwise it wouldn't work. That way you can't turn into a dragon w/o Paradox taking advantage of the Sanctum, and then get out to shit on Reality in your paradox-free dragon form.<br /> <br /> So, one could port this to all the world, and say that a Vulgar w/o Witness fireball can't be seen by witnesses w/o ceasing to exist before breaking Reality.<br /> <br /> The ST could determine that the fireball it's Vulgar w/o Witness, but also that it's going to fizzle if it risks to get out of the alley (or being seen other way)...unless it's casted as Vulgar with Witnesses, in which case it doesn't matter if someone get's to see the effect","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 09-18-2019, 01:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-18T10:21:25-07:00","id":1336589,"title":"","content":"After the fact Paradox isn't really a thing, the game has ways for magic to face consequences after being cast, but generally speaking if you cast something vulgar w/o witnesses, and before the spell ends a witness sees something, there's no increased risk of Paradox. Though it's worth noting that successfully casting a vulgar spell with or without witnesses has no difference to Paradox gained (in M20, in Revised with witnesses on a successful casting meant +1 point of Paradox), the big trouble is when you botch the roll to cast.<br /> <br /> Paradox is assessed as the spell is cast. Though it does not require the witnesses to see the mage, it requires them to see the spell. Just as it happens.<br /> <br /> To make it a bit easier, lets say a mage summons a lion out of thin air. This is obviously vulgar. If no witnesses see this, it's vulgar w/o witnesses. If someone sees a lion forming out of nothingness even if the mage is obscured, it's been witnessed. If someone sees someone gesticulating and muttering in a strange language, but never sees the lion coming into existence, it's not witnessed.<br /> <br /> Once the lion exists? Well then it's just a lion, and people are still going to react to there being a lion walking around, but the spell is done and safe. The mage might have some explaining to do about this later though.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-18T16:44:14-07:00","id":1336703,"title":"","content":"There's a skill literally for justifying what you do (did?) to avoid paradox, in M20. I forget the name.<br /> <br /> Which is weird because:<br /> Do I cast the spell, gain the paradox, and then it magic(k)ally goes away after I successfully convince someone that the fireball was just special effects?<br /> <br /> Or do I:<br /> Tell the ST I intend on justifying it, he accepts, I cast the spell, I use the skill, I succeed and don't get paradox at all<br /> <br /> Or something else?<br /> <br /> Also you gain paradox if your familiar is unnatural or does unnatural things. Your phoenix will generate you paradox everytime someone sees the bastard (Or I'd just keep it at once a scene).<br /> <br /> I think M20 also mentions gaining paradox everytime someone sees you do something unnatural. I assume the example would be something like:<br /> I cast a spell that lets me fly for a while. I get one paradox because that's not normal<br /> Everytime someone sees me fly I get another one.<br /> <br /> Which is really not that bad in the outdoors, hell maybe even being far enough away/dressed different wouldn't get you any 'that's just a UFO', but doing it in the city would probably make you explode.<br /> Which I think is kinda shitty and probably shouldn't be the hard-fast rule, seeing as I don't think other castings of that nature have the same effect. Why does flying in the city make me explode when casting fireball is just slightly higher difficulty. (Though the 'you fly in the city and explode' thing could be remedied by just a 'you can gain one more paradox per scene if a mundane sees you doing something unnatural')","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25315-jihelu","name":"Jihelu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-18T16:57:49-07:00","id":1336707,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25315-jihelu\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25315\" data-vbnamecard=\"25315\">Jihelu</a> its a little more then &quot;I just tell them its special effects&quot; you have to have the whole movie set, crew and kaboodle if you are whipping massive forces effects around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-18T17:01:08-07:00","id":1336709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jihelu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1336385-question-about-paradox-when-fighting-other-supernaturals-or-other-beings-of-strangeness?p=1336703#post1336703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a skill literally for justifying what you do (did?) to avoid paradox, in M20. I forget the name.</div> </div> </div> </div>Blatancy<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Tell the ST I intend on justifying it, he accepts, I cast the spell, I use the skill, I succeed and don't get paradox at all </div> </div> </div>Mostly this. You need to roll Blatancy first (keeping in mind that preparation is generally required for Blatancy, you need to arrange fro appropriate props and staging for people to fall for it). If you succeed, the spells is cast as coincidental, and follows the Paradox rules for coincidental magic (so none if you don't botch)<br /> <br /> In the fiction of what's happening this is all going on at the same time though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also you gain paradox if your familiar is unnatural or does unnatural things. </div> </div> </div>Are we using the full supplemental rules, or just M20 core?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think M20 also mentions gaining paradox everytime someone sees you do something unnatural. I assume the example would be something like: </div> </div> </div>Um... no?<br /> <br /> Long term magic that gives you obvious abilities like this result in things like permanent Paradox (it sits in your paradox pool even if your paradox roll would normally discharge it, until you end the spell) or Pattern Bleeding (need to spend quintessence or take damage until the effect ends, is more likely to be what you're thinking of) depending on the specifics.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-18T17:35:21-07:00","id":1336716,"title":"","content":"Turns out:<br /> The familiar = You get paradox because it shoots fire out of its mouth thing: I can't find it in M20 core, so it might be in Gods and Monsters or I'm pulling rules from fucking Forged in Dragons fire (I think it may be that book)<br /> <br /> For the other thing:<br /> Yeah I just thought wrong, perma-dox/bleeding is it.<br /> <br /> And not every explanation with Blatancy has to involve an entire stage be set up prior, one of the examples is just 'It's a flash mob'. Or even, although more difficult, 'It was an exploding gas main'. I imagine saying 'I'm gonna blow up the floor under someone and use the gas-main excuse' is going to get /really fucking old/ if you do it once every session.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25315-jihelu","name":"Jihelu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-18T17:55:17-07:00","id":1336723,"title":"","content":"The rules for it are flexible, but the &quot;flash mob&quot; needs... a flash mob; if you don't set it up, you're going to have to mind control a bunch of random people to make it look like a flash mob. You can't cover up a fireball with a flash mob because... they have nothing to do with each other.<br /> <br /> The Blatancy explanation has to actually explain things. The book is really emphatic about this. Blatancy rolls also get hard fast too. The gas-line thing? Base difficulty of 8, with a minimum of 2 successes, and the ST can call for more. Also, you have to be in a place where people at least think there's a gas main (that's part of the prop/prep thing... they aren't actually universal, and how much people know about these things depends a lot on where you are).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}